Heidelberger-Welch stationarity + halfwidth test (pvalue=.05, eps=.1):
--------------------------------------------------------------
Statistic       | Stationary    Start  Halfwidth   HW test
----------------+---------------------------------------------
edges           |     passed        1    24.1513    passed
mutual          |     passed        1     5.2923    passed
nodematch_prac  |     passed        1    19.8545    passed
nodeicov_seniority|     passed        1   754.7841    passed
gwesp_0.5       |     passed        1    47.9225    passed
--------------------------------------------------------------
Note: Stationary = passed a Cramer-von-Mises test on the chain's own cumulative-sum path (Heidelberger & Welch 1983), dis
> carding an increasing initial fraction (up to 50%) until it does - Start is the first retained iteration once it passes
> , FAILED means no discard fraction achieved stationarity. HW test additionally requires the retained portion's own 95% 
> CI halfwidth to be within eps() (default 10%) of its own mean - a separate, stricter precision check, only meaningful o
> nce stationarity itself has passed.

MCMLE's own convergence test was satisfied after   1 iteration(s).
Note: a satisfied convergence test is a necessary check, not proof of a converged fit - inspect the autocorrelation/ESS a
> bove, and consider increasing mcmcsamplesize()/mcmleiterations() if acceptance rate or ESS looks poor.

